  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 92b2c8003586277498a007ee213cc22b, type: 3}
  m_Name: 'Log - [unassigned 5]'
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::FloppyData
  diskName: 'Log - [unassigned 5]'
  logTitle: Unscheduled Transmission
  author: '[Captain TBD]'
  shipName: '[Unassigned]'
  dateRecorded: '[TBD]'
  logText: 'Received a transmission on the emergency frequency at approximately 0217.

    It
    lasted eleven seconds.

    At first I thought it was interference. A low, irregular
    sound, almost like someone breathing directly into a microphone.

    Then I
    heard a voice.

    Couldn''t understand what it was saying. It was too distorted,
    and there was a constant clicking sound underneath it.

    I tried responding,
    but the transmission stopped before I could establish contact.

    SYS-CTRL
    couldn''t identify the source. No nearby vessels, no detectable communications
    equipment, nothing.

    I replayed the recording several times.

    On the
    fourth attempt, I noticed something.

    There were two voices.

    One was
    speaking. The other was repeating the same sounds a moment later, almost perfectly.

    I
    don''t know what language they were speaking, or whether it was language at all.

    I
    tried playing it at a slower speed.

    I wish I hadn''t.

    The second
    voice wasn''t repeating the first.

    It was answering.'
